course: dictionary
lesson: 4367
title: Many meanings of one word
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: One word can have more than one meaning. The sentence around it tells you which meaning the writer chose. Gut can mean the tube in your body, or it can mean courage, or it can mean very disappointed.
explain: «Then she misses her mate's party because she has to mind the boys, and she's gutted (very disappointed).» The bracket gives you the meaning, and the reason, missing the party, shows why she feels that way. So gutted means very disappointed.
explain: «A tummy rumble is gas and liquid squeezed along the gut by its muscles, louder when the stomach is empty.» Here the clues are tummy and stomach, so gut means the tube inside your body where food travels.
explain: Always ask which meaning fits, then swap your meaning into the sentence and check that it still makes sense.
fact: The gut is the long tube in your body that food passes through, from the stomach to the intestines.
fact: A gut feeling is a strong feeling or idea you have without being able to explain why.
fact: Guts, in informal English, can mean courage, as in «have the guts to».
fact: Gutted, in UK informal speech, means very disappointed.
fact: Your gut holds trillions of useful bacteria, and fibre from fruit and vegetables helps keep it healthy.
exercise: What does gutted mean in «Then she misses her mate's party and she's gutted (very disappointed)»? | Covered in mud | Very full after a big meal | *Very disappointed | Very quick
exercise: Ella had a gut feeling that something was wrong, so she waited. What is a gut feeling? | *A strong feeling you cannot fully explain | A loud noise from somebody's stomach | A feeling in your tummy after eating too much | A feeling of being very tired
exercise: «A tummy rumble is gas and liquid squeezed along the gut by its muscles.» Which meaning of gut is used here? | Courage | *The tube that food passes through | Removing the insides of a fish | Very disappointed
test: What does guts mean in «She had the guts to say no to the bully»? | Brain power | Hunger | Insides of a fish | *Courage
test: What does it mean to gut a fish? | To wash it in the sink | *To take out its insides before cooking | To cook it whole in one piece | To put it in a tank
exam: Which sentence uses gut to mean the tube inside your body? | *A tummy rumble is gas and liquid squeezed along the gut | Monty is gutted | Have the guts to try | I had a gut feeling about the test
